re what money  laundering is that's okay let me break  this down for you money laundering is  where someone gets money whether it's  stealing or some other illegal way then  sends it through a bunch of different  channels and places so you can't tell  where that original money came from and  then that money eventually returned to  the original thief you might have heard  about it like the way i did when turkish  valorem players like cned were  questioned about their involvement in  this we touch on this do not jump to  conclusions right now so how did this  alleged money laundering scheme come to  light on october 23rd on the night  online forum a forum dedicated to the  mmorpg night online a document was  posted that compared the followings of  streamers the money that they made as  well as conversations with a quote bit  provider the post said that smaller  streamers were making insane amounts of  money via bits compared to their  viewership the numbers just didn't add  up the streamers were far too small to  be making so much money xenon explained  to me that the original post has been  deleted due to threats that were made  but it has been reposted a second time  with new names added this time no  conversations were included to help put  this in perspective according to middle  east eye quote some were found to be  earning up to eighteen hundred dollars a  day despite having just forty to fifty  viewers the money was being made through  bits if you're not sure where bits are  that's okay just know that one hundred  bits is equivalent to one us dollar you  donate bits and sometimes you get little  fun rewards from your streamers a skit a  gag or sometimes a sound queue whatever  basically it's like any other donation  with your money for those of you who are  not understanding why this is such a big  deal that is a crazy amount of money to  be making despite having such a small  amount of viewers after the initial  information came out a big streamer in  turkey named durane was made aware of  the list and tweeted about it on october  23rd including the claim that this was  happening via stolen credit cards duran  has about 600 000 followers on twitter  and 1.7 million on twitch cenon  explained to me that this is when the  story really began to spread durane's  tweet made people aware of the situation  beyond just the original post and the  night online players with so many  earnings not making sense and alleged  conversations about this donation  process people began to dig basically  there was some smoke and people began to  look for the fires duvar english the  english language source for turkish  online news site gazette duvar  specifically reported that according to  drain the streamer after receiving the  money pays their predetermined  commission generally 20 to 80 percent or  50 50 to launderers through the crypto  wallets so with this alleged scheme if  you were the perpetrator this is how it  all go down you would steal the credit  card information use that information  donate bits to a streamer that streamer  would send you some of the money back to  be clear i'm not saying to go out and do  this please do not commit crimes another  streamer named grimnax tweeted out  screenshots of discord messages which  allegedly showed discussion about the  money laundering scheme taking place  grimnax declined participating in the  scheme and then made a joke in the tweet  that he must have been a bad streamer  since he only offered him a 20 cut  another streamer quote tweeted gerain  and shared screenshots that seemed to  corroborate what drain was saying  showing discord messages that allegedly  show a conversation about bit donations  this tweet is from someone who allegedly  shows a credit card transaction that was  never authorized by them it's reported  that up to 10 million dollars was  laundered through this alleged scheme  duvar english also reported that in  another interview drain said that this  has been going on for years grimnak  seemed to confirm what duran said about  the length of time this has been  happening when they told the publication  middle east eye that quote this is  something that many of us have been  aware of for a long time but we couldn't  confirm twitch and the owner amazon nor  the audience for years we waited for the  prominent names on the platform to talk  about this issue as i mid-level  influencers like me weren't loud enough  so what has been the outcome of all of  this well a lot has happened since the  story first emerged so please bear with  me the calls for information and justice  actually grew to such a large size that  members of the turkish government began  to take notice politician names and i  apologize for butchering this name  gersol teching has called for  investigation and used the trending  hashtag hashtag temi's twitch or  cleantwitch another politician showed  support for the hashtag tami's twitch  movement on twitter a journalist also  reported that the parliament speaker  said they would be looking into the  events xenon told me that it looks like  an investigation was officially started  a twitch spokesperson also said in a  statement that quote recently members of  the twitch community have expressed  concerns toward the legitimacy of some  creators revenues in turkey we want to  assure our community that we do not  hesitate to take decisive action against  accounts engaged in prohibited conduct  we take efforts to combat and prevent  financial fraud on twitch on a regular  basis and in september alone we took  action against over 150 partners in  turkey for abuse of our monetization  tools duvar english have also since  reported that turkish schumer's  boycotted the platform until november  5th and that the rai games manager of  turkey said that they are aware and  monitoring the situation what started  out as just a forum post has become a  much bigger affair a turkish streamer  who was speaking about the situation p  queen said she was doxed live on stream  when someone donated bits and revealed  her phone number and her address super  massive blaze an organization that has a  prominent eu val roster announced that  they had parted ways with two players  but did not name them other orcs have  also parted ways with some of their  players related to the alleged scheme  xenon told me that acute streamers have  denied these allegations saying that  they were not aware of this stolen  credit card information a statement that  supports this was released by bbl lego  who has since been let go from his org  saying that he did participate in the  scheme but he was told it was completely  legal at first he then says he tried to  leave when the donor was anonymous but  he was unable to leave right away as his  growing popularity was used as blackmail  against him he also says that he was not  aware that the credit cards used were  stolen but what about cena like i said a  lot of you may have heard about this  story with the accusations being leveled  against him  was he accepting money from these  alleged money launderers and their  stolen credit cards his team ascend  which some of you may know as when the  16 teams competing in vct champions  released a statement regarding cnn's  involvement in the statement they said  that cena received one donation from an  account that has now since been  connected to the scheme they say that  cned was not in contact with the  perpetrator nor did he report the  donation to twitch which he now believes  was a mistake at the end of the day this  is all alleged there are no official  results for an investigation but if and  when those results become public we will  update you on them  i found xenon on twitter  and i just saw he worked for a turkish  esports outlet and i dm'd him and i was  like hey i should make sure i get this  right are you willing to speak to me  about this and he was so kind and so  patient and so understanding he he just  was translating things for me without me  asking this is a scene on stand club i'm  the president of the scene on stand club

